{% extends 'email/_layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
    <p style="margin: 0 0 20px 0;">Your sign-in code for N-Cards:</p>

    {# 与 de/ 那份逐行对应。改一边就要改另一边 —— MailTemplateRenderingTest 只能
       保证两边都渲染得出来，保证不了两边说的是同一件事。 #}
    <p style="margin: 0 0 20px 0; font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 32px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 6px; color: #18181b;">{{ code }}</p>

    <p style="margin: 0 0 24px 0;">The code is valid for <strong>{{ expires_in_minutes }} minutes</strong> and can only be used once.</p>

    {# ⚠️ T-106: This link does NOT consume the token (§7.1). See de/otp_code.html.twig
       for the full reasoning — enterprise mail gateways auto-GET every link, so the
       link points at a static landing page and the actual POST comes from the app. #}
    <p style="margin: 0 0 20px 0;">On your phone you can skip the typing:</p>

    <p style="margin: 0 0 24px 0;">
        <a href="{{ magic_link_url }}" style="display: inline-block; padding: 12px 24px; background-color: #18181b; color: #ffffff; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 600;">Continue sign-in</a>
    </p>

    <p style="margin: 0 0 20px 0; color: #71717a; font-size: 13px; word-break: break-all;">{{ magic_link_url }}</p>

    <p style="margin: 0 0 20px 0;">The code and the link belong to the same sign-in — once you have used one of them, the other stops working.</p>

    <p style="margin: 0;">Didn't request a sign-in? Just ignore this email. Without the code and without the link, nobody can sign in with your address.</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block footer %}
    <p style="margin: 0 0 8px 0;">We will never ask you for this code by email or by phone.</p>
    <p style="margin: 0;">This message was sent automatically. Replies are not read.</p>
{% endblock %}
